            "description": "Automated SOC Alert\n\n*Alert:* <<webhook.body.result.alert_name>> (<<webhook.body.result.mitre_id>>)\n*Severity:* <<webhook.body.result.severity>>\n*Account:* <<webhook.body.result.user>>\n*Service requested:* <<webhook.body.result.service>>\n*Source IP:* <<webhook.body.result.src_ip>>\n*Host (DC):* <<webhook.body.result.host>>\n*Time:* <<webhook.body.result.event_time>>\n\n*Threat Intel Enrichment*\n*VirusTotal:* malicious=<<DEFAULT(virustotal_ip.body.data.attributes.last_analysis_stats.malicious, \"n/a\")>> suspicious=<<DEFAULT(virustotal_ip.body.data.attributes.last_analysis_stats.suspicious, \"n/a\")>> harmless=<<DEFAULT(virustotal_ip.body.data.attributes.last_analysis_stats.harmless, \"n/a\")>>\n*VT owner / country:* <<DEFAULT(virustotal_ip.body.data.attributes.as_owner, \"n/a\")>> / <<DEFAULT(virustotal_ip.body.data.attributes.country, \"n/a\")>>\n*AbuseIPDB:* confidence=<<DEFAULT(abuseipdb_ip.body.data.abuseConfidenceScore, \"n/a\")>>% reports=<<DEFAULT(abuseipdb_ip.body.data.totalReports, \"n/a\")>> ISP=<<DEFAULT(abuseipdb_ip.body.data.isp, \"n/a\")>> country=<<DEFAULT(abuseipdb_ip.body.data.countryCode, \"n/a\")>>\n\n*Internal Context (last 24h)*\n<<DEFAULT(webhook.body.result.context, \"n/a\")>>\n*Distinct services requested:* <<DEFAULT(webhook.body.result.spns_24h, \"n/a\")>>\n_n/a means the source IP is internal or the lookup failed._",
            "issuetype": {
              "name": "Task"
            },
            "priority": {
              "name": "High"
            },
            "labels": [
              "Splunk-Alert",
              "ActiveDirectory",
              "<<REPLACE(webhook.body.result.mitre_id, \".\", \"_\")>>"
            ]
          }
        },
        "basic_auth": [
          "<<YOUR_EMAIL>>",
          "<<CREDENTIAL.jira_api_token>>"
        ]
